                "entry_id": "c3990388-126b-34da-8225-c0333a5c749e",
                "word": "makeweight",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c0f5cf48-1a40-46c8-8daa-32cd2545bbb6",
                        "entry_id": "c3990388-126b-34da-8225-c0333a5c749e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "makeweights"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "57155467-66d7-37f8-ac04-5d6f672e581a",
                        "entry_id": "c3990388-126b-34da-8225-c0333a5c749e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something of inferior quality which is included in a shipment to make up the weight."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e7e609e-cdc6-4b95-93ab-9bbf255b58f9",
                                "sense_id": "57155467-66d7-37f8-ac04-5d6f672e581a",
                                "text": "1893, Richard Le Gallienne, in a publisher's report on stories by Ernest Dowson, quoted in Jad Adams, Madder Music, Stronger Wine, page 88.\nI would advise you to accept these as an instalment of a volume, (they are not big enough to make one themselves) with the promise that the stories to come should be more striking, more original in theme — not less so, not mere makeweights — than those under consideration."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9643f30-bf1a-3505-a7aa-6ac013a66c50",
                        "entry_id": "c3990388-126b-34da-8225-c0333a5c749e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something included to add to the apparent weight or force of an argument."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10f58156-672b-484e-be42-d5eb44c719bd",
                                "sense_id": "a9643f30-bf1a-3505-a7aa-6ac013a66c50",
                                "text": "He added a long litany of peripheral precedents which the judge dismissed as mere makeweights."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae8fb330-b894-46c5-b0da-a1c638fd8a56",
                                "sense_id": "a9643f30-bf1a-3505-a7aa-6ac013a66c50",
                                "text": "Other railway schemes of the earliest period certainly mentioned benefits to agriculture, but only as a make-weight; most of them justified themselves by improved transport of minerals for shipment, […], or by carriage of bulk loads of manufactured goods."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be68cc33-5689-4b8f-af48-b82a3d56333c",
                                "sense_id": "a9643f30-bf1a-3505-a7aa-6ac013a66c50",
                                "text": "Fashion, as it happens, favors certain rows of the style matrix: museums, connoisseurs, and others are makeweights in the Artworld."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
